From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: add the camera subsystem and CCI

Add the two CCI controllers and the CAMSS node to sm8350.dtsi, disabled,
as sm8250.dtsi does. Addresses, interrupts and clocks come from the stock
devicetree of the Galaxy Z Flip3. Compared with SM8250 there is a third
full IFE at 0xacef000 (CSID interrupt 640, IFE interrupt 641), all six
CSIPHY regions are 0x2000 long, and CSIPHY4 uses interrupt 122.

CCI0 drives gpio107 to gpio110 and CCI1 gpio111 to gpio114, with pull-up
when active and pull-down when suspended, as in the stock pin states.
Stock runs both controllers at 37.5 MHz, which is the source rate the
driver timing table for CCI v2 is written for, so assign that rate the
way sm8650.dtsi does.

The IFE stream IDs (0x800, 0x840, 0xc00 and 0xc40, mask 0x440) are
copied from the stock camera SMMU context bank. SM8250 lists eight IDs
with mask 0x400; whether SM8350 needs more than the stock set under
mainline has not been checked on hardware yet.

The CCI blocks are the same v2 controller as on SM8250, so document
qcom,sm8350-cci with the qcom,msm8996-cci fallback and the five SM8250
clocks.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
